#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119514 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/id #uuid "8235213e-4e88-57f6-89b0-de589ad2b38d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4418" :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "The $4$th row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3 \\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-8)+(0-0) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119515 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column"}] :question/id #uuid "6f0a6499-03db-5833-b175-4835325d34d6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4419" :question/problem "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119584 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a88f6712-2115-55ce-abe4-b3c27e2e105f" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/id #uuid "5cc1443c-03cd-5f86-bcfc-b9b7f4c6a565" :question/math-academy-id "e-5182" :question/problem "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-6)\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+1\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a88f6712-2115-55ce-abe4-b3c27e2e105f" :knowledge-point/title "Applying a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96c49654-3888-5875-ad69-4fa09baf0fe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309811} {:answer/id #uuid "62f1a025-1a55-59ce-885a-2a84ec2d3842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309812} {:answer/id #uuid "964a4d46-2921-5d79-bc85-3eb425c3856b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309813} {:answer/id #uuid "b06bc4d4-62e2-5b4d-8b88-aa98855c5d50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309814} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9f433c-9c97-5eca-aa6d-ce60fbcccd73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 